        "transcript": [
          "Speaker 1 @0.0s [en]: Good morning, everyone. Thanks for joining the weekly planning meeting for the mobile app redesign.",
          "Speaker 2 @5.5s [en]: Morning. I reviewed the design files yesterday and I have a few concerns about the onboarding flow.",
          "Speaker 1 @12.7s [en]: Okay, let's start there. What is the main problem you noticed?",
          "Speaker 2 @18.5s [en]: The sign-up screen asks for too much information up front. Most people will abandon it before they finish.",
          "Speaker 1 @27.5s [en]: That makes sense. Could we move the profile questions to a later step, after the first login?",
          "Speaker 1 @43.2s [en]: Then let's decide that the sign-up screen will only collect email and password.",
          "Speaker 2 @50.5s [en]: Agreed. I will update the wireframes and share them with the team before Thursday.",
          "Speaker 1 @56.5s [en]: Perfect. The next topic is the notification settings. Customers keep asking for a quiet mode during the weekend.",
          "Speaker 2 @65.3s [en]: We could add a simple toggle in the settings page. It should be easy to build.",
          "Speaker 1 @72.1s [en]: I like that idea, but we need to check with the backend team about scheduling.",
          "Speaker 2 @80.8s [en]: I can talk to Omar about it this afternoon, and I will report back tomorrow.",
          "Speaker 1 @86.5s [en]: Thank you. Another item is the performance of the dashboard.",
          "Speaker 1 @90.0s [en]: It still takes several seconds to load on older phones.",
          "Speaker 2 @93.6s [en]: I measured it last week. Most of the delay comes from loading every chart at the same time.",
          "Speaker 1 @100.2s [en]: So should we load the charts only when the user scrolls to them?",
          "Speaker 2 @104.9s [en]: Exactly. Lazy loading should cut the waiting time roughly in half.",
          "Speaker 1 @111.0s [en]: All right. Let's make lazy loading the priority for the next sprint.",
          "Speaker 2 @116.5s [en]: Sounds good. Should we also invite the support team to the next review?",
          "Speaker 2 @124.3s [en]: Yes, please send them an invitation. Their feedback about customer complaints would be really helpful.",
          "Speaker 2 @132.0s [en]: Will do. Is there anything else we need to cover today?",
          "Speaker 1 @137.0s [en]: I think that is everything. Thanks everyone, and see you next week."
        ]
      },
